      "description": "Which member is legal on a given entry is decided by RC-1 (native-evidence.md section 4.3) and is NOT schema-decidable: applicability is total over the registered (relation, rung) pairs and turns on membership of the RUNG in the closed five-member resolved set (resolved-target, resolved-binding, resolved-callee, checked, from-resolved-calls), never on the relation ladder length. A resolved rung must never be not-applicable - reachability@from-resolved-calls is a one-rung relation whose single rung IS resolved - and every other registered rung, including unresolved-edge@observed and types@annotated as well as the syntactic rungs, is not-applicable with attempted=false, unresolvedEdgeCount=0 and unresolvedEdgeClasses=[]. RC-0 runs first and is relation-specific: the pair must be registered, meaning the rung is a member of THAT relation's own ladder, so unresolved-edge@enumerated is refused although both tokens are registered. That check and the not-applicable minting law (attempted false, count 0, empty class list) are enforced by coverage_bijection at the producer boundary AND again at retained Run closure, and they hold for a FACT-FREE entry over an empty examined scope. not-applicable is never a fallback for an unregistered pair. stageTerminal is deliberately not constrained: a not-applicable entry may retain the stage terminal its producer observed.",
